                <pb facs="0898" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg778"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Eddy to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic">November 2,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Eddy reports the situation improving. The general strike will come to an end
                    to-morrow. It is hoped that railway communication will be open within a few
                    days. Small disturbances continue and the revolutionary party is still active.
                    The situation in Finland is serious.</p>
            </div>
